  "district": "3rd Congressional District",
  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Maryland's 3rd Congressional District, which covers all of Howard County and parts of Anne Arundel and Carroll counties, will elect a U.S. Representative on November 3, 2026. The seat is currently held by first-term Democrat Sarah Elfreth, who won a contentious 22-candidate open primary in 2024 and the general election. Elfreth faces primary challengers including progressive Austin Dyches, Jennifer Cross, and Sean Hammond, while Republicans Ray Bly, Berney Flowers, Felix Seier, and John White compete in their primary on June 23, 2026. The district leans strongly Democratic, and the general election is expected to be rated as Solid or Safe Democratic by nonpartisan forecasters.",
