      "name": "Sarah Elfreth",
      "party": "Democratic",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Sarah Elfreth is the incumbent U.S. Representative for Maryland's 3rd Congressional District, first elected in 2024. She previously served six years in the Maryland State Senate representing Anne Arundel County's District 30, where she chaired a budget subcommittee and passed 91 bipartisan bills. Elfreth holds a bachelor's degree from Towson University and a master's in public policy from Johns Hopkins University, and has focused on protecting federal workers, supporting veterans, and addressing affordability.",
